    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0340" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-29T17:00:00+03:25">March 29, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. Reference to my 61 of March 11, 5 p.m., the Prime Minister informs me the
                    Cabinet at last night’s meeting formally agreed to expel the Japanese Legation.
                    Japanese Minister will be informed of this action within next few days.</p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s 66, March 13, 6 p.m.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d381-f1"/>
                    and my 84,<anchor n="87" xml:id="d381-f2"/> Prime Minister feels it would
                    strengthen his hand in explaining this action to Majlis if he could announce
                    some concrete indications of American economic assistance particularly if he
                    could make public the extension of Lend-Lease aid to Iran.<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d381-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
